# OSRS Ironman Progression Planner — Phase 5 review package

Replacement P5-002 is delivered for independent reviewer, CEO review and Owner acceptance under ADR-025. Phases 1–4 are Owner-accepted; Phase 6 is NOT AUTHORIZED. This is a local-first statically deployable personal planner. Manual statuses and canonical hard-only prerequisites remain independent; no automatic game prerequisites or completion propagation.

## Run on Windows

From this existing application folder run npm run dev and keep the terminal open. Use http://127.0.0.1:4173/ with the same browser/origin for your saved roadmap. No package install is required. Export JSON regularly; source files alone do not back up browser IndexedDB. Do not rebuild the preserved dist by default. Current separate review build: evidence/p5-002-2026-10-27T15-45-40-716Z/static/ under the same server.

## Daily controls

- Click a graph goal to select; double-click for quick title/category/manual-status editing. Manual status is displayed; edit it in quick/details/Board controls (also keyboard accessible). Empty click clears temporary selection; drag empty space to pan, wheel to zoom. Fit and Optimize are explicit.
- Double-click empty canvas for catalog search beside a prominent Create custom goal button. Custom opens title/category directly; switch paths without losing typed fields, or confirm replacing them with a catalog choice. More details transfers draft/reference/position to the optional inspector. Notes, icons and detailed grouping stay there. Panel toggle/view switching preserves notes. Inspector Cancel discards unsaved form changes and closes; replacing another dirty draft still requires confirmation.
- Drag right + to left input for connections, or click source then Shift-click destination and Connect. Required prerequisite blocks readiness; Recommended preparation and Preferred order never block. Status remains manual even when prerequisites disagree.
- Shift-drag empty canvas to select full visible cards. The counted Status/Group/More/Clear toolbar previews affected IDs; hidden/unselected members and downstream goals are never implicit. Undo/Redo uses the same state across Graph and Board.
- Board has three manual-status columns and shared quick edits. Combine goal-name/category/readiness/group filters; completed goals remain searchable. Clear filters restores results. Graph hiding/Focus/group collapse never changes Board's canonical readiness. Last view/Board filters and graph viewport survive reload/backups.
- Right-click or Shift+F10 opens contextual actions; Escape cancels a quick surface or clears selection. Tab/Enter access status and editor controls. Only More details explicitly opens the inspector.
- Numeric progress UI is Owner-hidden throughout the application; stored values and validation/backups remain intact. Restoring its UI requires Owner approval.
- Save status and Retry remain visible in both views. Help / Diagnostics includes controls, failure injection for disposable tests, and catalog source/permission notices. Import previews/requires export of the current roadmap and explicit replacement confirmation. Failed writes preserve the prior committed copy; Retry before reloading unsaved work.

## Reference content and permissions

207 factual reference records: 24 skills, 32 quests, 30 items, 24 bosses, 29 prayers, 48 diary tiers and 20 activities. These are a documented subset/snapshot, not all game content or requirements. 94 pinned authentic PNGs total 60,053 bytes: 90 identity-specific matches and 117 disclosed generic category markers. Original symbols remain available. Owner reports private-local Jagex permission; not independently verified and no broader distribution rights implied. See catalog/ARTWORK.md for pins, notices, coverage and preparation. Unknown/missing icons fall back without deleting references. Two goals from one reference remain independent; catalog updates never overwrite player edits/state.

Read [catalog provenance/import/coverage](catalog/README.md), [asset permission manifest](catalog/asset-manifest.json) and [source review](catalog/source-review.json). Run node scripts/import-catalog.mjs catalog/reference-source.json --check to verify the generated catalog. This tool is offline and never accesses a player's roadmap.

## Consolidated Owner walkthrough

1. Run npm run dev in the existing checkout and use http://127.0.0.1:4173/. Use a disposable browser profile for acceptance; export personal work before replacement. No install is needed. The separately verified build is evidence/p5-002-2026-10-27T15-45-40-716Z/static/ beneath the same origin. Do not run the default build over preserved dist.
2. On a graph goal, double-click for quick editing or use keyboard/context Open details. Change manual status, Cancel, then apply. Selection, positions and connection pairing must stay unchanged. Undo/Redo, reload and switch to Board: the same goal/ID changes, independently of downstream goals. No numeric progress controls or values should appear in either view or any editor/menu/help.
3. Double-click empty canvas, use default catalog search for Cook's Assistant and filter Quest. Also try the adjacent Create custom goal path. Create it twice; complete/edit one and verify the other remains independent. More details preserves the reference, draft and intended canvas position. Use manual/custom entry for gaps. In details, change a local icon override; unknown or missing assets must fall back.
4. In Board, combine name/category/readiness/group filters; verify completed search, Ungrouped, clearing filters and reload/JSON preferences. Test a literal group ID null in disposable JSON: it must not include ungrouped goals. Hidden/collapsed prerequisites still determine canonical hard-only readiness.
5. Enter unsaved notes in Board details, close it, switch to Graph, single-click a different goal, and reopen details. Original notes must remain without a prompt. Opening another object's details or applying a conflicting edit still asks before discarding. Decline and verify both drafts remain.
6. Optimize a disposable branching roadmap, reload and move a goal manually. Verify readable reconstructed routes without changing IDs/relationships or other positions. Exact raid metrics and screenshots are in the evidence. Export/reload/restore including stored fractional progress, and use Help / Diagnostics to test failed save/Retry and failed import replacement. Test artifacts include a real changed-catalog build proving user data survives an update.

## Validation and limits

93/93 Node checks and 47/47 current browser/build groups passed with disposable Chrome data. See [TEST_REPORT.md](TEST_REPORT.md), [HANDOFF.md](HANDOFF.md), [testing inventory](docs/TESTING.md) and [phase gate](docs/agents/CURRENT_PHASE_GATE.md). The documented raid reconstruction now has zero measured crossings/shared segments in compact/detailed reload/manual-move fixtures; no universal guarantee for overlapping/non-planar graphs or production-scale performance is claimed. The clarified Owner notes-switching report did not reproduce; Owner verification remains part of acceptance. Individual live audit of all catalog links, unique artwork for 117 category-marked entries, mobile, other browsers and Phase 6 hardening remain gaps/unrun. Historical records and pre-P5 README remain preserved in evidence.
